@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Daily Grind security audit and deployment
+
+The audit covered all HTML, CSS, package configuration, and the HTTP handler.
+There are no client-side scripts, third-party JavaScript libraries, DOM injection
+sinks, cookies, postMessage handlers, forms, popups, or embeds in this repository.
+The only external dependency is the existing Unsplash CSS background image.
+The original page had an inline stylesheet and style attribute; both now live in
+`styles.css`. The original server supplied no security headers.
+
+## Implemented protections
+
+- Enforced CSP denies scripts, inline styles, connections, plugins, workers, and
+  other unspecified resources. Local CSS and images from `images.unsplash.com`
+  are allowed. Base tags and framing are blocked; forms are limited to this origin.
+- Trusted Types enforcement and `trusted-types 'none'` prevent DOM injection
+  sinks and creation of permissive policies in supporting browsers. No sanitizer,
+  client script, or compatibility shim is needed for this script-free page.
+  Older browsers still receive CSP protection where supported.
+- MIME sniffing, framing, unnecessary device permissions, cross-origin resource
+  reads, and referrer disclosure are restricted. COOP uses
+  `same-origin-allow-popups`; no COEP or cross-origin isolation is needed.
+- Fetch Metadata rejects cross-site subresource requests while preserving top-level
+  links and clients without these headers. Reports are exempt because browsers
+  deliver them separately. No permissive CORS headers are added.
+- Logout sends `Clear-Site-Data` and `Cache-Control: no-store`. This prototype has
+  no authentication or sessions to invalidate; a future authenticated application
+  must invalidate sessions server-side and protect state-changing actions from CSRF.
+
+## Safe rollout
+
+The audited, script-free site defaults to enforcement. For a deployment with
+additional integrations, set `SECURITY_POLICY_MODE=report-only` to dry-run the full
+CSP and Trusted Types policy while retaining enforced framing/base/plugin protection.
+Set `SECURITY_REPORT_ORIGIN=https://your-public-host.example` to enable the modern
+`Reporting-Endpoints` destination. It must be an HTTPS origin without a path,
+credentials, query, or fragment. The relative `report-uri /security-reports` is
+also provided for browsers using legacy reporting. No untrusted Host or forwarded
+headers determine the reporting destination.
+
+Review reports over representative production traffic (days to weeks), classify
+extension noise, and fix legitimate dependency violations before reverting the
+mode to enforcement. Keep reporting enabled after promotion. The collector logs
+only an allowlisted directive and disposition; URLs, samples, user agents, and
+other arbitrary fields are discarded. It accepts the two browser report formats,
+limits request bodies to 16 KiB, and considers at most 20 reports per request.
+Treat reports as untrusted signals, not proof of an attack or complete coverage.
+At the deployment edge, rate-limit `/security-reports`, set request timeouts, and
+exclude report bodies and query strings from access/error logs. `report-sample`
+can include code fragments in incoming reports; never retain raw bodies.
+
+Terminate HTTPS at the production edge. After verifying HTTPS for the public host,
+set `ENABLE_HSTS=true` to begin with `max-age=300`; increase it only after stable
+operation. Subdomain inclusion and preload are intentionally deferred until all
+affected hosts have been audited. Configure the edge to preserve these response
+headers on all routes, including errors, and avoid conflicting duplicate policies.
+Changing back to report-only does not remove CSP already cached by an external CDN;
+purge such cached HTML when changing deployment policies.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run `npm test` for handler tests with in-memory request/response objects and
+`npm run build` for syntax checks. Neither command starts a server or imports
+`server.js`. Tests cover policy-compatible markup, stylesheet MIME type, policy
+modes, report privacy and rejection cases, Fetch Metadata, and logout headers.
+No browser verification or live deployment verification was performed.
